  "result": "I added a `--json` flag to the `quote` command. It prints `{\"total_cents\": N}`, and without the flag the output is the same as before. All 7 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`).\n\n- **`shop/cli.py`**: the flag is a plain on/off option. With it, the command prints the total in cents as JSON; without it, it prints the formatted amount as before. `calc_total` already returns an integer, so N is a whole number of cents.\n- **`tests/test_cli.py`** (new, since there were no CLI tests): `test_quote_json` runs `quote --json a:10.00:2` and checks the parsed output is `{\"total_cents\": 2165}`.\n\nWhen I called `main()` directly, the default output was `21.65` and the JSON output was `{\"total_cents\": 2165}`. Note that `python3 -m shop.cli quote ...` prints nothing, because `cli.py` has no `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block. That was already the case before this change.",
